{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\Books\\6th\\Math\\JPG\\008.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "1.2.1IndexNotation", "conf": 0.847, "box": [[99, 128], [550, 125], [550, 164], [99, 167]]}, {"text": "Do you know what index notation means?", "conf": 0.898, "box": [[351, 266], [1115, 254], [1115, 296], [351, 309]]}, {"text": "The index of a number represents how many times a", "conf": 0.931, "box": [[424, 423], [1403, 404], [1404, 449], [425, 469]]}, {"text": "number is multiplied by itself. It is a small raised number", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[425, 482], [1466, 461], [1467, 507], [426, 528]]}, {"text": "written next to the number which is being multiplied by", "conf": 0.908, "box": [[422, 538], [1449, 523], [1449, 568], [422, 582]]}, {"text": "itself.Indexisalso calledpower/exponent.", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[422, 600], [1197, 590], [1197, 630], [422, 640]]}, {"text": "Look at 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2.", "conf": 0.752, "box": [[92, 694], [592, 688], [592, 725], [92, 731]]}, {"text": "QuickCheck", "conf": 0.857, "box": [[1156, 695], [1370, 691], [1370, 731], [1156, 735]]}, {"text": "It canbewrittenin indexformorinpower/exponentas:", "conf": 0.937, "box": [[90, 751], [1102, 746], [1102, 786], [90, 791]]}, {"text": "Write the following in index notation:", "conf": 0.884, "box": [[1172, 768], [1720, 762], [1720, 798], [1172, 804]]}, {"text": "'2×2×2×2×2×2 = 26", "conf": 0.78, "box": [[190, 813], [646, 804], [647, 847], [191, 856]]}, {"text": "a)3×3×5×5", "conf": 0.81, "box": [[1174, 820], [1392, 815], [1393, 848], [1175, 853]]}, {"text": "Here 2 is called the base and 6 is called the index or", "conf": 0.864, "box": [[89, 873], [1025, 867], [1025, 906], [89, 913]]}, {"text": "b)2×2×7×11×11×13", "conf": 0.862, "box": [[1173, 867], [1556, 861], [1556, 896], [1173, 903]]}, {"text": "power. 2° represents that number 2 is 6 times multiplied", "conf": 0.932, "box": [[90, 931], [1116, 921], [1116, 970], [90, 979]]}, {"text": "by itself. We can read 2° as 2 to the power of 6.", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[91, 989], [931, 985], [931, 1031], [91, 1035]]}, {"text": "In 2°, 2 is called base and 6 is called exponent.", "conf": 0.89, "box": [[88, 1042], [925, 1046], [925, 1095], [88, 1091]]}, {"text": " Example 3:", "conf": 0.871, "box": [[36, 1145], [303, 1166], [299, 1223], [32, 1203]]}, {"text": "Write primefactors of 3408.Express the'factors'in index notation.", "conf": 0.904, "box": [[90, 1229], [1309, 1237], [1309, 1280], [90, 1272]]}, {"text": "21", "conf": 0.56, "box": [[185, 1312], [243, 1312], [243, 1355], [185, 1355]]}, {"text": "3408", "conf": 0.584, "box": [[254, 1311], [346, 1311], [346, 1354], [254, 1354]]}, {"text": "Step I: First we break 3408 into its factors as: 2 ×x 1704", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[586, 1330], [1609, 1336], [1609, 1378], [586, 1372]]}, {"text": "1704", "conf": 0.726, "box": [[257, 1373], [348, 1373], [348, 1412], [257, 1412]]}, {"text": "Step ll: Now we break 1704 into its factors as: 2 × 852", "conf": 0.878, "box": [[587, 1393], [1600, 1402], [1600, 1444], [587, 1435]]}, {"text": "852", "conf": 0.645, "box": [[277, 1435], [350, 1435], [350, 1477], [277, 1477]]}, {"text": "Step Ill: Now we break 852 into its factors as: 2 × 426", "conf": 0.879, "box": [[588, 1456], [1591, 1467], [1591, 1509], [588, 1497]]}, {"text": "426", "conf": 0.75, "box": [[275, 1496], [351, 1499], [350, 1544], [274, 1541]]}, {"text": "StepIV:Nowwebreak426 into itsfactorsas:2×213", "conf": 0.899, "box": [[588, 1519], [1591, 1533], [1591, 1574], [588, 1561]]}, {"text": "213", "conf": 0.749, "box": [[278, 1563], [352, 1566], [350, 1610], [276, 1608]]}, {"text": "StepV:Nowwebreak 213 intoitsfactorsas:3×71", "conf": 0.909, "box": [[590, 1583], [1549, 1597], [1549, 1637], [590, 1623]]}, {"text": "71", "conf": 0.665, "box": [[305, 1636], [355, 1636], [355, 1679], [305, 1679]]}, {"text": "Now 3and 71 areprime factors so, we stop here.", "conf": 0.906, "box": [[590, 1644], [1502, 1662], [1501, 1705], [589, 1686]]}, {"text": "3408=2×2×2×2×3×71", "conf": 0.802, "box": [[98, 1734], [602, 1745], [601, 1780], [97, 1770]]}, {"text": "Here2 is repeated 4 times.So we can write it as:", "conf": 0.866, "box": [[97, 1792], [962, 1811], [961, 1850], [96, 1831]]}, {"text": "3408 = 24×3×71", "conf": 0.831, "box": [[96, 1843], [422, 1851], [421, 1894], [95, 1885]]}, {"text": "QuickCheck", "conf": 0.873, "box": [[1141, 1836], [1366, 1841], [1365, 1882], [1140, 1876]]}, {"text": "Here3408 isthe standard form,2×2 ×2×2×3×71", "conf": 0.86, "box": [[96, 1904], [1049, 1930], [1048, 1970], [95, 1944]]}, {"text": "Findtheprimefactorsandwrite", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[1154, 1905], [1664, 1920], [1663, 1956], [1153, 1941]]}, {"text": "is the expanded form and 2* × 3 × 71 is the index form.", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[95, 1962], [1087, 1984], [1086, 2027], [94, 2005]]}, {"text": "the following in index notation:", "conf": 0.901, "box": [[1153, 1954], [1653, 1971], [1652, 2006], [1152, 1990]]}, {"text": "a)5662b)45981", "conf": 0.904, "box": [[1154, 2003], [1437, 2011], [1436, 2047], [1153, 2039]]}, {"text": "CHING", "conf": 0.752, "box": [[138, 2088], [197, 2080], [200, 2104], [141, 2112]]}, {"text": "Share following online game with students to practice prime factorization", "conf": 0.911, "box": [[252, 2102], [1365, 2135], [1364, 2175], [251, 2142]]}, {"text": "https://www.mathplayground.com/factortrees.html", "conf": 0.909, "box": [[255, 2141], [1022, 2164], [1021, 2206], [254, 2184]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.858, "box": [[1287, 2338], [1637, 2352], [1636, 2391], [1286, 2377]]}]}